1431:+  # population that chose not to have them. CEREMONY_EFFECTIVE is the ONE
1432:+  # resolution of the ceremony in this script (recorded install-state, then
1433:+  # --ceremony, then CEO_UPGRADE_CEREMONY, then the fail-safe `user`); this
1434:+  # function CONSUMES it. Only the literal `maintainer` selects the wider
1435:+  # template; every other value — including unset, which only a harness can
1436:+  # produce — takes the narrower one, the same fail-SAFE direction the
1437:+  # resolution itself chose.
1438:+  #
1439:+  # And INFERRED is not RECORDED (rail round 8, P1). With no readable
1440:+  # install-state and no --ceremony, the resolver above answers `user` only as
